# known-failures.allow — the PostgreSQL regression-suite ratchet ledger.
# Companion: scripts/rowsort_compare.py --allow-file. Precedent:
# crates/_support/seams_init/tests/lint-determinism.allow.
#
# One overlaid test name per line. A listed test may fail without failing CI;
# a test NOT listed that fails breaks the build, and a listed test that starts
# PASSING is reported stale and also breaks the build, so this file can only
# shrink. Removing an entry is the unit of progress.
#
# SEED: 2026-09-04, first execution of the vendored suite (submodule pinned to
# REL_18_3 = 62d6c7d3df6287f1bd83199c1a746e50d31571a0) against a pgrust server
# built from main @ 489c1fc542. pg_regress raw: 157/230 "failed", but 136 of
# those were the overlay's own -- pgrust:rowsort marker echo, which this
# comparator strips. Real residual: 17 fail + 1 error, seeded below.
#
# Clusters, for whoever picks these up:
#   generated columns   — output stops early (~900 deleted lines, 0 added):
#                         reads as an unported feature or an aborting error,
#                         not a wrong answer.
#   COPY                — copy/copy2/copyselect/compression.
#   partitioning/planner— mixed +/-, consistent with plan-shape divergence from
#                         the redesigned executor. feat/pgbackrest-compat has
#                         two written adjudications of exactly this territory
#                         (ADJUDICATION-PARALLEL-PLAN-SHAPE.md,
#                         ADJUDICATION-PORTALS-CURSOR-ORDER.md) not on main.
#   security            — privileges, rowsecurity.

alter_table
compression
copy
copy2
copyselect
generated_stored
generated_virtual
join
limit
partition_aggregate
partition_join
partition_prune
portals
privileges
rowsecurity
select_distinct
subselect

# error, not a diff: produced no output at all on the seed run.
numeric_big
